    "status": "VISIBLE SPORE DEPOSIT",
    "sourceLine": "SOURCE IMAGES: Source photograph: bn5-f56.jpg | Microscope record: objective/magnification ______ mount/stain ______ spores measured (n) ______ image filename __________________",
    "summary": {
      "Growth / description": "Small pale fungal fragment or compact basidiome section with a smooth cream interior and a thin darker outer margin.",
      "Size": "Small fragment; no calibrated scale visible. Direct measurement required.",
      "Color": "Interior white to cream; outer edge light tan to brown.",
      "Cap / Pileus": "2.1",
      "Hymenophore": "No intact fertile surface is visible clearly enough to characterize gills, pores, teeth, or other hymenophore structure.",
      "Spores": "No controlled spore print documented. Microscopy required.",
      "Stem / Stipe": "No intact stipe visible.",
      "Veil": "No identifiable veil structures visible.",
      "Base / Substrate": "A small dark attachment or soil-stained area is present on one edge; substrate association remains uncertain.",
      "Microscopy record": "Use the source microscope record fields; no microscopic identification has been inferred in this atlas.",
      "Source completeness note": "Additional field image not embedded in this source record",
      "Additional master notes": "[[PB_BN5FIELD001]]BN5-FIELD-001 PHOTOGRAPHIC FIELD RECORD — VOUCHER STATUS UNCONFIRMED IMAGE PLATE — FIELD SERIES [[BN5FIELD001_IMG01]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG02]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG03]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG04]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG05]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG06]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG07]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG08]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG09]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG10]] [[BN5FIELD001_IMG11]] GROWTH / DESCRIPTION Extensive polyporoid colony forming numerous thin, sessile, imbricate brackets densely distributed over decorticated and bark-bearing woody substrate. Pilei range from small developing shelves to broad fan-shaped brackets and show pronounced concentric zoning. Several views reveal pale gray, cream, tan and warm buff bands with a conspicuous pink-lilac to violet marginal zone. The fertile undersurface appears darker violet-brown in several oblique views and is finely poroid to locally irregular/irpiciform at the resolution available. Macromorphology is consistent with a violet-zoned Trichaptum-like polypore morphotype; species-level determination is intentionally withheld because no voucher identity, microscopy, or controlled spore data accompany this field series. SIZE No calibrated scale is visible. Colony occupies a large continuous area of the photographed trunk; direct dimensions of individual brackets and total colony extent are not available from the images alone. COLOR Upper surfaces pale gray to gray-brown, cream, buff and tan in concentric bands; active margins whitish to pink-lilac or violet. Lower/fertile surfaces visible in oblique views are violet-brown to dusky purple. Green patches on some upper surfaces are consistent with superficial algal or moss colonization. CAP / PILEUS Pilei thin, tough-appearing, sessile, semicircular to flabelliform, densely overlapping and strongly concentrically zoned. Surfaces appear finely tomentose to velvety with radial fibrillose texture in close view. Margins are thin, wavy to lobed, and distinctly paler with lilac-violet edging. HYMENOPHORE True lamellae are absent. Exposed undersides are dark violet-brown and appear finely poroid, with portions becoming irregular to tooth-like/irpiciform. Pore density, tube depth and microscopic hymenial structures cannot be measured from these field photographs. SPORES No controlled spore print or microscopy is linked to this photographic field record. Basidiospore dimensions, basidia, cystidia/setal elements, hyphal system, clamp connections and reagent reactions remain pending. STEM / STIPE No differentiated stipe is present; fruit bodies are laterally attached and sessile. VEIL No annulus, volva or veil structures are present or expected for this polyporoid morphotype. BASE / SUBSTRATE Fruit bodies arise directly from dead or declining woody tissue on a large trunk. Host tree identity is not established from the supplied images. White fungal growth and areas of decorticated wood are present around portions of the colony. RECORD STATUS Photographic field record only. No specimen label is visible in this image series, and the photographs cannot be defensibly assigned to an existing numbered BN5 voucher solely by macromorphologic similarity. Voucher/collection status therefore remains unconfirmed pending field notes or specimen cross-reference. SOURCE IMAGES IMG_2677.jpg; IMG_2678.jpg; IMG_2679.jpg; IMG_2680.jpg; IMG_2681.jpg; IMG_2682.jpg; IMG_2683.jpg; IMG_2684.jpg; IMG_2685.jpg; IMG_2686.jpg; IMG_2687.jpg MICROSCOPY: none linked to this field-only record. ________________ [[PB_AFTER_BN5FIELD001]]BN6 | 35 specimens"
    },
